===Etymology===
{{calque|en|nl|stilleven}}.

===Noun===
{{en-noun|s|still lives}}

# {{lb|en|painting}} A [[work of art]] [[depict]]ing an [[arrangement]] of [[inanimate]] [[object]]s.
# {{lb|en|cellular automata|usually|countable}} A [[pattern]] that does not change from one [[generation]] to the next.
#* {{quote-newsgroup|en|date=1992-05-05|author=Holocaust-->Travesty|title=the Hodge Podge machine|newsgroup=comp.theory.cell-automata|url=https://groups.google.com/g/comp.theory.cell-automata/c/W-wTpza_q1s/m/F2o9fEirjSwJ|text=I think you're talking about a configuration known as "eater," a '''still life''' in 6-8 cells. If the glider hits the right spot, the eater will form a bridge and destroy the glider while undergoing little change before reverting.}}
#* {{quote-newsgroup|en|date=1996-11-16|author=Paul Callahan|title=Still-life glider reflector found|newsgroup=comp.theory.cell-automata|url=https://groups.google.com/g/comp.theory.cell-automata/c/sHpFoieXvk4/m/NQRWMvcD76oJ|text=Thus, a natural question, apparently proposed very early, was whether there exists a '''still life''' (i.e. period 1 oscillator) that reflects a glider.}}
#* {{quote-newsgroup|en|date=2003-12-12|author=Tony Finch|title=Implementing Conway's Life|newsgroup=comp.theory.cell-automata|url=https://groups.google.com/g/comp.theory.cell-automata/c/chyMzRsH41c/m/2-pZ4Tjk7tMJ|text=I haven't tested yet, but I expect hlife to win by a very large margin since the puffer train has lots of '''still life''' and blinkers to make Gosper's algorithm look good, and hlife's low-level implementation is quite good at handling the more random parts.}}

